WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.112
By the end of this module, you should be able to identify long and wide structures,

00:00:04.112 --> 00:00:08.522
pivot and unpivot data in PostgreSQL, and explain the grain of each result.

00:00:08.522 --> 00:00:15.462
You should also be able to detect when a reshape changes more than structure because aggregation or a join has

00:00:15.462 --> 00:00:15.907
altered the facts.

00:00:15.907 --> 00:00:19.752
Finally, you should be able to choose a shape based on what happens next: visualization, reporting,

00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:25.252
or modeling. Keep a real project in mind as we work through this section—for example,

00:00:25.252 --> 00:00:29.627
a survey project reshaping question responses for analysis.

00:00:29.627 --> 00:00:33.617
The technical feature matters because it changes what questions we can answer reliably and how easily another

00:00:33.617 --> 00:00:36.442
analyst can understand our work.

00:00:36.442 --> 00:00:41.782
As you listen, try to connect each SQL or data concept to a decision you might need to defend later:

00:00:41.782 --> 00:00:45.617
what the data means, what one row represents, what can be missing,

00:00:45.617 --> 00:00:48.000
and what assumptions the transformation introduces.
